From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anonymous <anonymous@localhost>
Date: Fri, 02 Oct 2026 04:45:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] trackers: per-tracker HTTP queues, down-tracker
 detection, pooled curl transport

HTTP(S) announces and scrapes went through one global FIFO limited by
max_concurrent_http_announces, each on its own connection with
"Connection: close". A slow or unreachable tracker held slots until its
requests timed out, and every other tracker's requests waited behind it.

tracker_manager now queues HTTP requests per tracker (scheme, host, port,
local address) and starts them round-robin between trackers. The number
in flight per tracker adapts: it starts at 4, grows by one per success
while requests are waiting (by about one per round trip after the first
failure), halves on failure, and is capped by
tracker_host_max_concurrency. "stopped" announces may use up to
tracker_stopped_concurrency. After tracker_failure_threshold failures in
a row (connect, TLS, timeout, HTTP 5xx) a tracker is treated as down:
its requests fail right away, and one request at a time is let through
after a back-off (10 s, doubling up to 5 minutes).

With -Dcurl-trackers=ON and tracker_http_pool (default on), requests go
through libcurl's multi interface on the network thread: connections are
kept alive and reused per tracker, and HTTP/2 is negotiated where the
tracker offers it (tracker_http2), multiplexing requests over one
connection. Name resolution, SSRF mitigation, the IP filter and listen
socket routing stay in libtorrent; curl only connects to the filtered
addresses, and redirects are followed by libtorrent. A SOCKS4, SOCKS5 or
HTTP tracker proxy is used by curl as well (connections stay pooled
through it); names are resolved and filtered by libtorrent as before,
except with SOCKS5 and proxy_hostnames, where the proxy resolves them.
i2p keeps using http_connection.

Requests wait in their tracker's queue (also while it is down) for at most
tracker_queue_timeout seconds; then they fail and the torrent retries on its
own schedule. A queued request whose listen socket closed (the listen port or
interfaces changed) is dropped, and a tracker's queue holds at most
tracker_host_max_queue requests.

New settings: tracker_http_pool, tracker_http2,
tracker_host_max_concurrency (32), tracker_host_max_streams (250),
tracker_stopped_concurrency (256), tracker_failure_threshold (5),
tracker_connect_timeout (10), tracker_queue_timeout (600),
tracker_host_max_queue (20000).
